  "analysis": "In the thymus, T cell precursors undergo a process of maturation that includes both positive and negative selection. During positive selection, which occurs in the cortex of the thymus, T cells must bind to MHC molecules on cortical epithelial cells to survive. At this stage, the T cells express both CD4 and CD8 co-receptors, making them double-positive (CD4+ and CD8+). This is a well-established aspect of T cell development, where the double-positive T cells that successfully bind to MHC molecules are selected for further maturation. The T cells that do not bind undergo apoptosis. Therefore, the best description of the T cells during this phase of differentiation is 'CD4+ and CD8+' (option opa).",
